  <media:group>
   <media:title>Hyundai Translocal Series: Via Satellite l Artist Teaser l Jane Jin Kaisen</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/q9HBxGoJNe4?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i2.ytimg.com/vi/q9HBxGoJNe4/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>Artist Jane Jin Kaisen works across experimental film, installation, performance, and text to explore memory, migration, borders, and translation. Her work considers how human experience intersects with larger social, cultural, and natural forces, often engaging with island geographies, cosmologies, myths, and ritual and spiritual practices.

For &quot;Hyundai Translocal Series: Via Satellite,&quot; a collaboration between Nam June Paik Art Center and Pinacoteca de São Paulo, the artist turns to the moon, ocean currents, and tides as natural forces that connect people across different places and cultures. Her new work reflects on cycles of time and imagines forms of connection that extend across geographic boundaries, tracing how nature has brought people together since long before the development of modern technologies.

Stay tuned for the opening of &quot;Hyundai Translocal Series: Via Satellite&quot; on November 5 at the Nam June Paik Art Center and on November 28 at the Pinacoteca de São Paulo.

