   <media:title>Hyundai Translocal Series: Via Satellite l Artist Teaser l biarritzzz</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/BRo7BKKW4g4?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i3.ytimg.com/vi/BRo7BKKW4g4/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>biarritzzz, currently based in Salvador, works through and across disciplines to trace the overlaps between media, pop music, language, and code. The self-described transmedia and anti-disciplinary artist deconstructs forms and formats to foreground counter-narratives.

For &quot;Hyundai Translocal Series: Via Satellite,&quot; a collaboration between Nam June Paik Art Center and Pinacoteca de São Paulo, the artist looks to the word “samba.” While the term names a musical genre and dance tradition rooted in Afro-Brazilian culture, biarritzzz explores language and its layered meanings. In collaboration with choreographer, dancer, and musician Tsumbe Maliya, she traces how the word has traveled through time and space and transformed through the body, image, and emerging visual cultures.

Stay tuned for the opening of &quot;Hyundai Translocal Series: Via Satellite&quot; on November 5 at the Nam June Paik Art Center and on November 28 at the Pinacoteca de São Paulo.

