  <media:group>
   <media:title>Hyundai Translocal Series: Via Satellite l Artist Teaser l Vivian Caccuri</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/xtuxMa-5770?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i1.ytimg.com/vi/xtuxMa-5770/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>Vivian Caccuri creates installations, performances, and musical compositions that challenge familiar ways of listening and perceiving the world. Drawing on sound as both material and method, the Rio de Janeiro-based artist reveals hidden relationships between bodies, technologies, and environments.

For &quot;Hyundai Translocal Series: Via Satellite,&quot; a collaboration between Nam June Paik Art Center and Pinacoteca de São Paulo, the artist turns her attention to the mosquito as a point of connection between biology, sound, and colonial history. Through this unexpected figure, her new work reflects on how humans have sought to understand, classify, and shape the natural world, and how these ideas continue to resonate today.

Stay tuned for the opening of &quot;Hyundai Translocal Series: Via Satellite&quot; on November 5 at the Nam June Paik Art Center and on November 28 at the Pinacoteca de São Paulo.

